  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_baldachin_cb580681004c6256e62ba60f0c51e1d28ad83b054794b71e4968e1322bd5244b80">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a rich silk brocade (OED s.v. baldachin, Heyd 686-7) | Canopies over such features as thrones, altars, tombs, or doorways; may be suspended, projecting, or free-standing." [Source: Getty AAT] | a rich embroidered stuff, originally woven with woof of silk and warp of gold thread; rich brocade. (OED s.v. baldachin, Heyd, 686-7) | Canopies over such features as thrones, altars, tombs, or doorways; may be suspended, projecting, or free-standing. [Source: Getty AAT]</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
